      "message": "IIUC, the anchor thingy exists to rebuild block mapping?\n\nIn the stage2_set_owner() case, force_pte\u003dtrue which makes stage2_leaf_mapping_allowed() return always false.\n\nCouldn\u0027t we use this mechanism instead? having force_pte\u003dfalse for the reclaim portion? That would avoid having to detect in the common pgtable code if we are 1. on the reclaim path 2. on the host stage-2 pgtable?\n\nstage2_leaf_mapping_allowed() could be aware of the refcount and would let the PRE callback destroy the mapping when appropriate?",
